  "claim": "An opera was written by the German poet born in the Kingdom of Bohemia, also referred to by the name German Kingdom. Renée Fleming performed in this opera.",
  "evidencia": "Page: Jaroslav Kvapil. Sentence: Jaroslav Kvapil (25 September 1868 in Chudenice, Kingdom of Bohemia – 10 January 1950 in Prague) was a Czech poet, playwright, and librettist.\nPage: Kingdom of Bohemia. Sentence: The Kingdom of Bohemia, sometimes in English literature referred to as the Czech Kingdom (Czech: \"České království\" ; German: \"Königreich Böhmen\" ; Latin: \"Regnum Bohemiae\" , sometimes Latin: \"Regnum Czechorum\" ), was a medieval and early modern monarchy in Central Europe, the predecessor of the modern Czech Republic.\nPage: Rusalka (opera). Sentence: 114, is an opera ('lyric fairy tale') by Antonín Dvořák.\nPage: Renée Fleming. Sentence: Her signature roles include Countess Almaviva in Mozart's \"Le nozze di Figaro\", Desdemona in Verdi's \"Otello\", Violetta in Verdi's \"La traviata\", the title role in Dvořák's \"Rusalka\", the title role in Massenet's \"Manon\", the title role in Massenet's \"Thaïs\", the title role in Richard Strauss's \"Arabella\", the Marschallin in \"Der Rosenkavalier\", and the Countess in \"Capriccio\".",
  "evidence_text": "Page: Jaroslav Kvapil. Sentence: Jaroslav Kvapil (25 September 1868 in Chudenice, Kingdom of Bohemia – 10 January 1950 in Prague) was a Czech poet, playwright, and librettist.\nPage: Kingdom of Bohemia. Sentence: The Kingdom of Bohemia, sometimes in English literature referred to as the Czech Kingdom (Czech: \"České království\" ; German: \"Königreich Böhmen\" ; Latin: \"Regnum Bohemiae\" , sometimes Latin: \"Regnum Czechorum\" ), was a medieval and early modern monarchy in Central Europe, the predecessor of the modern Czech Republic.\nPage: Rusalka (opera). Sentence: 114, is an opera ('lyric fairy tale') by Antonín Dvořák.\nPage: Renée Fleming. Sentence: Her signature roles include Countess Almaviva in Mozart's \"Le nozze di Figaro\", Desdemona in Verdi's \"Otello\", Violetta in Verdi's \"La traviata\", the title role in Dvořák's \"Rusalka\", the title role in Massenet's \"Manon\", the title role in Massenet's \"Thaïs\", the title role in Richard Strauss's \"Arabella\", the Marschallin in \"Der Rosenkavalier\", and the Countess in \"Capriccio\".",
