        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "c64f08f0-2d41-515e-ad79-61361bb78144",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Jaroslav Kvapil, Antonín Dvořák, Renée Fleming, Wolfgang Amadeus Mozart, Giuseppe Verdi, Jules Massenet, Richard Strauss\n- Places: Chudenice, Prague, Kingdom of Bohemia, Central Europe, Czech Republic\n- Works: Rusalka, Le nozze di Figaro, Otello, La traviata, Manon, Thaïs, Arabella, Der Rosenkavalier, Capriccio\n- Roles: Countess Almaviva, Desdemona, Violetta, Marschallin, Countess\n- Topics: Czech literature, opera\n\nFacts:\n- Jaroslav Kvapil was born on 25 September 1868 in Chudenice in the Kingdom of Bohemia.\n- The Kingdom of Bohemia was a medieval and early modern monarchy in Central Europe and was the predecessor of the modern Czech Republic.\n- Rusalka is an opera described as a lyric fairy tale by Antonín Dvořák.\n- Jaroslav Kvapil was a Czech poet, playwright, and librettist.\n- Renée Fleming's signature roles include the title role in Antonín Dvořák's Rusalka.\n- Renée Fleming's signature roles also include Countess Almaviva in Mozart's Le nozze di Figaro, Desdemona in Verdi's Otello, Violetta in Verdi's La traviata, the title roles in Massenet's Manon and Thaïs, the title role in Richard Strauss's Arabella, the Marschallin in Der Rosenkavalier, and the Countess in Capriccio.\n- Jaroslav Kvapil died on 10 January 1950 in Prague.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "e85d9c09-81f2-5e84-add1-bf1394dddf6d",
        "text": "Page: Jaroslav Kvapil. Sentence: Jaroslav Kvapil (25 September 1868 in Chudenice, Kingdom of Bohemia – 10 January 1950 in Prague) was a Czech poet, playwright, and librettist.\nPage: Kingdom of Bohemia. Sentence: The Kingdom of Bohemia, sometimes in English literature referred to as the Czech Kingdom (Czech: \"České království\" ; German: \"Königreich Böhmen\" ; Latin: \"Regnum Bohemiae\" , sometimes Latin: \"Regnum Czechorum\" ), was a medieval and early modern monarchy in Central Europe, the predecessor of the modern Czech Republic.\nPage: Rusalka (opera). Sentence: 114, is an opera ('lyric fairy tale') by Antonín Dvořák.\nPage: Renée Fleming. Sentence: Her signature roles include Countess Almaviva in Mozart's \"Le nozze di Figaro\", Desdemona in Verdi's \"Otello\", Violetta in Verdi's \"La traviata\", the title role in Dvořák's \"Rusalka\", the title role in Massenet's \"Manon\", the title role in Massenet's \"Thaïs\", the title role in Richard Strauss's \"Arabella\", the Marschallin in \"Der Rosenkavalier\", and the Countess in \"Capriccio\".",
